# Shipmate Security Rules (Cursor `.mdc`)

Enforce these security invariants on every edit. Full rule docs: https://shipmate.agency/rules/

- **Supabase & Postgres RLS:** Every `CREATE TABLE` in `public` MUST include `ALTER TABLE ... ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;` in the same migration. Never use `USING (true)` or `WITH CHECK (true)` on `ALL`/`INSERT`/`UPDATE`/`DELETE` policies (a policy with no `FOR` clause is `ALL`). Use `WITH (security_invoker = true)` on client-facing views.
- **No client-exposed secrets:** Never place `service_role`, Stripe secrets, webhook secrets, or LLM API keys in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, `VITE_*`, or browser bundles. Keep `.env` in `.gitignore`.
- **Auth on every mutation:** Treat every Next.js Server Action (`"use server"`) and `/api/*` route as a public HTTP endpoint; verify server session and resource ownership on the server.
- **Signed Stripe webhooks only:** Read raw `await req.text()` and validate via `stripe.webhooks.constructEvent(rawBody, sig, secret)` before changing billing entitlements.
- **Bounded AI spend:** Require auth, rate limits, and an explicit output-token cap (`max_tokens` / `max_output_tokens`) on every LLM proxy route.
- **Local scan:** Run `shipready_scan_repo` before merging to production.
